# Root build-context exclusions.
#
#   This file is only consulted when a build uses the repository root as its
#   context. docker-compose.yml builds with the contexts "backend" and
#   "frontend", which have their own .dockerignore files -- so nothing here
#   affects `docker compose build` today. It exists so that a future
#   root-level `docker build .` does not ship the whole repo into an image.
#
#   Patterns use **/ because a bare name like "node_modules" only matches at
#   the context root, and the real directories live one level down
#   (frontend/node_modules, backend/__pycache__, ...).

# Version control and repo metadata
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
test-prompts/

# Docker and compose files are not needed inside the image
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose*.yml

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dependencies
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]

# Build output
**/dist
**/build
**/*.egg-info

# Test, coverage and type-checker output
**/coverage
**/htmlcov
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*

# Local databases
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3-journal
**/*.db

# Logs
**/logs
**/*.log
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/pnpm-debug.log*

# Documentation
#   backend/.dockerignore and frontend/.dockerignore both drop README.md, so
#   keep the root file consistent with them. **/ is required: a bare *.md
#   matches only at the context root, not backend/README.md.
**/*.md

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/

# OS files
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
